course: dictionary
lesson: 2880
title: One word, many doors
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word door is a small word with several meanings. Its main meaning is a part of a wall that opens and closes so people can go in and out of a room, house or car. «Then Mum saw the glow under her door.» Here the door is the part of the wall that opens, and the glow is coming through the gap under it.
explain: A door can also be a small hinged part of a cupboard, oven or fridge. «An open oven door and the inside of the oven are hot enough to burn skin instantly.» Here the door is the oven's hinged part, and it can be very hot. Always check the sentence to see which door is meant.
explain: Some phrases use door in a special way. «Next door» means in the house beside yours. «Door to door» means from one house to the next, or all the way. «Out of doors» means outside, so the words in a sentence show you the meaning.
fact: A door is a part of a wall that opens and closes.
fact: A cupboard, oven or fridge can have a small hinged door too.
fact: «Next door» means in the house beside yours.
fact: «Door to door» means from one house to the next, or all the way.
fact: Doors can be dangerous. «A family in Ohio left a pan of oil on the hob and went to answer the door; it caught fire, and when someone threw water on it a ball of flame burst up and burnt the kitchen.» Never throw water on a pan fire, and always get a grown-up.
exercise: What is a door? A part of a wall that opens and closes so people can go in and out | A window that opens and closes | *A part of a wall that opens and closes so people can go in and out | A kind of floor covering
exercise: «Next door» means what? | *The house beside yours | A car parked outside | A cupboard in the kitchen | The room at the top of the stairs
exercise: Why must you be careful near «an open oven door»? | It is too light to hold | It stops the kitchen from being warm | It can make a loud noise like a bell | *It is hot enough to burn your skin instantly
test: What does «door to door» mean? | Under the table | Inside a single room only | *From one house to the next, or all the way | Only on Sundays
test: In «qǐng jìn» (ching JIN), what does the host mean when they say it at the door? | Go out now | Come back tomorrow | Shut the door | *Come in, please
exam: What does «out of doors» mean? | *Outside | Behind a wall | Next to the oven | Inside a cupboard
